  <h1>Frontend Real-Time URL Route Search & Pagination System</h1>

  <div class="meta-box">
    <strong>Project:</strong> Family Together Sanctuary Platform (Frontend & Backend)<br>
    <strong>Module:</strong> Full-Stack Pagination, Live Route URL Synchronization & Debounced Search<br>
    <strong>Target Repositories:</strong> <code>family-together-frontend</code> & <code>family-together-backend</code><br>
    <strong>Status:</strong> <span class="badge badge-success">Production Ready</span><br>
    <strong>Date of Implementation:</strong> September 2026
  </div>

  <h2>1. Overview & Architecture</h2>
  <p>
    This documentation details the complete design and implementation of real-time search typing synchronization in browser route URLs, coupled with server-side pagination across the frontend application.
  </p>
  <p>
    When users search for records (family members, memories, documents, upcoming events, access invitations, or user accounts), two critical UX challenges occur:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Live URL Synchronization:</strong> The browser URL address bar immediately reflects the user's keystrokes in real time (e.g., <code>?tab=members&search=john</code>) so URLs are shareable, bookmarkable, and history-navigable.</li>
    <li><strong>Focus & Performance Protection:</strong> Standard router pushes (like Next.js <code>router.push()</code> or <code>router.replace()</code>) cause client router re-evaluations, losing input cursor focus and stuttering user typing. This was solved by using synchronous <code>window.history.replaceState()</code> while keeping query parameters preserved.</li>
    <li><strong>Network Optimization:</strong> Keystroke queries to the RTK Query backend are debounced by <strong>300ms</strong>, avoiding network request flooding while the address bar updates immediately.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout callout-success">
    <strong>Key Innovation:</strong> Keystrokes update the browser URL bar instantaneously without page flickering or cursor focus loss, while server requests fire 300ms after the user finishes typing.
  </div>

  <h2>2. The Reusable Hook: <code>usePaginationSearch</code></h2>
  <p>
    Located in <code>src/hooks/usePaginationSearch.ts</code>, this custom React hook encapsulates all route parameter parsing, real-time URL updates, state synchronization, and debouncing.
  </p>

  <h3>2.1 Hook Interface & Signature</h3>
  <pre>
export interface UsePaginationSearchOptions {
  defaultLimit?: number;       // Default items per page (e.g. 6, 9, 10)
  searchParamKey?: string;     // URL parameter name (default: "search")
  pageParamKey?: string;       // URL parameter name (default: "page")
  limitParamKey?: string;      // URL parameter name (default: "limit")
  debounceMs?: number;         // Milliseconds to debounce backend query (default: 300)
}

export function usePaginationSearch(options?: UsePaginationSearchOptions): {
  searchTerm: string;          // Current value in the search input
  debouncedSearch: string;     // Debounced query value passed to backend API
  page: number;                // Current active page index (1-indexed)
  limit: number;               // Current page size
  setSearchTerm: (valueOrEvent: string | React.ChangeEvent&lt;HTMLInputElement&gt;) =&gt; void;
  setPage: (newPage: number) =&gt; void;
  setLimit: (newLimit: number) =&gt; void;
  clearSearch: () =&gt; void;
}
  </pre>

  <h3>2.2 Synchronous Route Synchronization</h3>
  <p>
    When a user types into any search bar, <code>setSearchTerm</code> immediately executes:
  </p>
  <pre>
const updateUrlRouteImmediately = useCallback(
  (newSearch: string, newPage: number, newLimit?: number) =&gt; {
    if (typeof window === "undefined") return;

    // Preserves all existing query params (e.g., ?tab=members, &from=tree, etc.)
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

    if (newSearch && newSearch.trim()) {
      params.set(searchParamKey, newSearch);
    } else {
      params.delete(searchParamKey);
      params.delete("q");
    }

    if (newPage &gt; 1) {
      params.set(pageParamKey, String(newPage));
    } else {
      params.delete(pageParamKey);
    }

    const queryString = params.toString();
    const updatedUrl = queryString ? `${pathname}?${queryString}` : pathname;
    
    // Updates browser address bar instantly without reloading or dropping input focus
    window.history.replaceState(null, "", updatedUrl);
  },
  [pathname, searchParamKey, pageParamKey, limitParamKey, defaultLimit]
);
  </pre>

  <h2>3. The UI Component: <code>PaginationControls</code></h2>
  <p>
    Located in <code>src/components/common/PaginationControls.tsx</code>, this component provides accessible, high-contrast pagination controls.
  </p>
  <h3>Features:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dynamic Range Display:</strong> Displays exact item boundaries (e.g., <em>"Showing 1 to 9 of 45 records"</em>).</li>
    <li><strong>Smart Windowing:</strong> Intelligently renders page buttons (<code>1, 2, 3 ... 10</code>) when total pages exceed visible threshold.</li>
    <li><strong>Quick Navigation:</strong> Includes first page (<code>&laquo;</code>), previous page (<code>&lsaquo; Prev</code>), next page (<code>Next &rsaquo;</code>), and last page (<code>&raquo;</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Per-Page Limit Selector:</strong> Optional dropdown for 10, 20, or 50 items per page.</li>
    <li><strong>Automatic Zero-State Hide:</strong> Gracefully hides controls when total results is zero.</li>
  </ul>

