  <h2>5. Backend API Query Integration</h2>
  <p>
    The backend NestJS controllers were previously upgraded with <code>PaginationQueryDto</code> and custom query DTOs:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>GET /family/members?page=1&limit=9&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /family/memories?page=1&limit=6&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /family/documents?page=1&limit=9&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /family/events?page=1&limit=6&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /family/invitations?page=1&limit=8&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /family/activity-logs?page=1&limit=8&search=...</code></li>
    <li><code>GET /users?page=1&limit=10&search=...</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every endpoint returns a unified standard envelope:
  </p>
  <pre>
{
  "data": [ /* Array of records */ ],
  "meta": {
    "total": 42,
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "totalPages": 5,
    "hasNextPage": true,
    "hasPrevPage": false
  }
}
  </pre>
  <p>
    In RTK Query (<code>familyApi.ts</code> and <code>adminApi.ts</code>), the <code>transformPaginatedList</code> helper automatically attaches <code>.meta</code> to the returned array so existing components that iterate over the array continue working seamlessly without any breaking changes!
  </p>

  <h2>6. Quality Verification & Test Results</h2>
  <div class="callout callout-success">
    <strong>TypeScript Verification:</strong> <code>npx tsc --noEmit</code> passed with <strong>0 errors</strong>.
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Live Typing:</strong> Address bar updates synchronously with each keystroke (e.g., <code>?tab=members&search=john</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Back/Forward Navigation:</strong> Clicking the browser's Back and Forward buttons syncs the search input and pagination controls without desynchronization.</li>
    <li><strong>Query Parameter Preservation:</strong> Switching between tabs preserves <code>tab</code>, <code>action</code>, and other essential dashboard state.</li>
    <li><strong>Zero State Handling:</strong> Informative, friendly empty states with a "Clear search" action when no items match the query.</li>
  </ul>

